      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I had hacked the sksl-\u003emsl code generation to emit `const constant FSUniformData\u0026` when it saw this variable declaration and it actually negatively impacted performance. I think that was causing it de-reference the SSBO address every time we\u0027d access a field, vs. reading it into the stack/registers once.\n\nWhere I think we do want reference support is when we then pass this local struct into the emitted helper functions. For now, most (all?) shaders seem to have the helper functions get inlined away so it doesn\u0027t matter. It would also be nice to use references for when accessing a snippet sub-struct from this struct and invoking the static module functions. Since the module functions aren\u0027t always inlineable, I think that\u0027s where it could matter.",
      "parentUuid": "22d2394a_ac2adbad",
